## Report
Crash/valgrind/debugger attempts were blocked by build constraints. `cargo test -p server list_objects_delimiter_unbounded_fetch -- --nocapture` failed because Cargo could not download `tiny_http` (403 from crates.io) and offline mode reports the package missing. `valgrind --version` and `gdb --version` are not available; lldb is present but there is no built test binary to debug due to the dependency fetch failure. 

Code review confirms the DoS vector: `Coordinator::list_objects_v2` sets `per_pg_limit` to `u32::MAX` whenever `delimiter.is_some()` and passes that to each PG list request, then collects all PG responses into `all_objects` before sorting/dedup and only later applying delimiter/max_keys truncation (coordinator.rs:438-470). The storage layer derives the SQL LIMIT directly from `req.max_keys` (`limit = req.max_keys as i64 + 1`) and eagerly pushes all rows into a `Vec` before truncating to `req.max_keys` (pg_store.rs:392-534). With `u32::MAX`, this becomes an effectively unbounded LIMIT (~4.29e9), so a delimiter listing can force full-bucket enumeration and large memory allocations despite small `max_keys`, validating the availability risk described.

